# What the app image's build may see (BuildKit reads this file because it sits next to deploy/docker/Dockerfile and has
# its name plus .dockerignore). It is an allow-list: everything is left out first, then the folders the app needs are
# let back in. A folder added to the repository later is NOT shipped until it is listed here; tests/packaging fails
# and names it, so nothing is left out or put in by accident. Local, private or generated files (output/, node_modules/,
# a workspace, .git) can never reach the image this way.
*
# The code and what it reads at run time
!apps
!core
!src
!examples
!fonts
!docs/assets/icon.svg
!docs/assets/logo-light.svg
!docs/assets/logo-dark.svg
# The license, and the licenses of what Offerowl uses, in the image as in the package
!LICENSE
!docs/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
# The typesetting libraries are installed from these two files
!package.json
!package-lock.json
# The command line, started by the container as `offerowl`
!offerowl
# The render container: the self-test (offerowl selftest) fingerprints its recipe and its starter (src/resume.py:
# SELFTEST_INPUTS). Inside this image they are only read.
!render
# The container's entrypoint
!deploy/docker/entrypoint.py

# Left out of the folders above: caches and generated files
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
examples/interview/out
fonts/.uuid
